=base:main-content.cmark

# Changelog: tramaj-purs

Release history of `tramaj-purs`, the reference PureScript implementation: parser, evaluator, Node codec and analyses. Releases happen when there are
major changes rather than on a schedule; each entry below is one version.
Every implementation has its own page like this one, and each page is
tagged so the site builds one Atom feed per implementation:
#changelog #purescript #tramaj-purs

The unreleased entry has breaking changes to numbers:
[Migrating to integers and floats](/migrating-to-integers-and-floats.html)
says what to do about each.

=base:main-content.tramaj-doc
@version=import("changelog/version", {"package": "tramaj-purs"})
.div(class: "changelog",
  $version({
      "version": "(none)",
      "date": "unreleased",
      "summary": "Consumed as a git dependency; no registry release yet.",
      "changes": [
          {
              "kind": "added",
              "text": "Reference implementation of the language: parser, evaluator (concrete and symbolic modes), normative Node JSON codec and static analyses."
          },
          {
              "kind": "added",
              "text": "Conformance corpus under \`corpus/cases\`, shared with every other implementation."
          },
          {
              "kind": "added",
              "text": "Object destructuring patterns in \`@\` bindings and lambda parameters (decisions section 17): a parser lowering to plain \`Let\`/\`Lambda\`, checked by shared corpus cases 100-118."
          },
          {
              "kind": "changed",
              "text": "Breaking: numbers are two types, an integer and a float (decisions section 18). A literal and a JSON number are typed by their text: \`3\` is an integer, \`3.0\` and \`3e0\` are floats. Integers cover -(2^53 - 1) to 2^53 - 1; an integer outside that range is a parse error as a literal and a \`TypeMismatch\` in the context."
          },
          {
              "kind": "changed",
              "text": "Breaking: a number keeps its type when written. \`str(1.0)\` is \`1.0\` where it was \`1\`, and every JSON boundary writes a float with a fraction or an exponent."
          },
          {
              "kind": "changed",
              "text": "Breaking: \`eq\` never equates an integer with a float, and \`lt\`/\`lte\`/\`gt\`/\`gte\` take two integers or two floats; a mixed pair is a \`TypeMismatch\`."
          },
          {
              "kind": "changed",
              "text": "Breaking: \`Tramaj.Json\` replaces \`Data.Argonaut.Core.Json\` in the public API, with a reader and a writer that keep the type of a number."
          },
          {
              "kind": "changed",
              "text": "Breaking: \`\"$term\"\` is a reserved object key, and \`int\` and \`float\` replace \`number\` as v4 type primitives."
          },
          {
              "kind": "added",
              "text": "The arithmetic profile: \`sum\`, \`product\`, \`negate\`, \`quotient\`, \`inverse\`, \`floor-quotient\`, \`modulo\`, \`floor\` and \`real\`, and the \`NotRepresentable\` error. It is off by default: \`evalProgramWith\` and \`runProgramWith\` take an \`Options\` record that turns it on."
          },
          {
              "kind": "added",
              "text": "Terms: over a symbol an arithmetic builtin evaluates to \`{\"$term\", \"arguments\"}\`, with its operands as written."
          },
          {
              "kind": "added",
              "text": "\`arithmeticOps\` and \`deepArithmeticOps\`, the arithmetic names a program references."
          }
      ]
  }).rendered)

